CLASS:: WSOLAStretchShift
summary:: Waveform-similarity overlap-add time-domain pitch shifter
categories:: UGens>Pitch
related:: Guides/PitchShiftSuite, Classes/PitchShift, Classes/OLAStretchShift, Classes/SpectralHybridShift

DESCRIPTION::
WSOLAStretchShift is a Waveform-Similarity Overlap-Add pitch shifter based on the algorithm by Verhelst & Roelands. Unlike standard granular pitch shifters that splice grains at fixed intervals, WSOLA searches within a tolerance window for the optimal grain splice location using waveform cross-correlation. Splicing grains only where waveforms are in-phase prevents phase cancellation and amplitude flutter, producing smooth and natural time-domain pitch shifting with very low latency.

Processing is monophonic; multichannel expansion applies over Arrays.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate mono input signal.

ARGUMENT:: ratio
Pitch ratio multiplier (0.5 to 2.0). Default is 1.0.

ARGUMENT:: grainSeconds
Grain duration in seconds (scalar, default 0.04).

ARGUMENT:: overlaps
Number of overlapping grains (scalar integer, default 4).

ARGUMENT:: window
Grain envelope window shape (scalar: 0 = Hann, 1 = Triangular). Default is 0.

returns:: An audio-rate pitch-shifted signal.

EXAMPLES::

SUBSECTION:: Synthetic Signals

code::
// 1. Monophonic Sine: plays original (220 Hz) then pitch-shifted (ratio 1.5, +7 semitones)
(
fork {
    // Original
    x = {
        var sig = SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 0.1);
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 0.1);
        var shifted = WSOLAStretchShift.ar(sig, 1.5);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)

// 2. Polyphonic Chord: plays original chord then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    // Original chord
    x = {
        var sig = Mix(SinOsc.ar([220, 277.18, 329.63], 0, 0.05));
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted chord
    x = {
        var sig = Mix(SinOsc.ar([220, 277.18, 329.63], 0, 0.05));
        var shifted = WSOLAStretchShift.ar(sig, 1.5);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)

// 3. Percussive / Transient: plays original bursts then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    // Original bursts
    x = {
        var sig = PinkNoise.ar(0.1) * Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(4), 0.005, 0.15);
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted bursts
    x = {
        var sig = PinkNoise.ar(0.1) * Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(4), 0.005, 0.15);
        var shifted = WSOLAStretchShift.ar(sig, 1.5);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Recorded Audio

code::
// 4. Monophonic Recorded Sound (Guitar): original, then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    var buf = Buffer.read(s, Platform.userExtensionDir +/+ "PitchShiftSuite/HelpSource/Audio/PitchShiftSuite/guitar-monophonic.wav");
    s.sync;

    // Original
    x = { PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2) ! 2 }.play;
    buf.duration.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2);
        WSOLAStretchShift.ar(sig, 1.5) ! 2;
    }.play;
    (buf.duration + 0.2).wait;

    buf.free;
};
)

// 5. Polyphonic Recorded Sound (Piano Chords): original, then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    var buf = Buffer.read(s, Platform.userExtensionDir +/+ "PitchShiftSuite/HelpSource/Audio/PitchShiftSuite/piano-polyphonic.wav");
    s.sync;

    // Original
    x = { PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2) ! 2 }.play;
    buf.duration.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2);
        WSOLAStretchShift.ar(sig, 1.5) ! 2;
    }.play;
    (buf.duration + 0.2).wait;

    buf.free;
};
)
::
